  "supremeCourt": {
    "name": "Supremo Tribunal Federal (STF)",
    "size": 11,
    "appointmentMethod": "Nominated by the President, confirmed by the Senate; mandatory retirement at 75.",
    "fspEraChanges": "No structural change to the court. PT presidents (Lula, Dilma) filled vacancies through the normal process. As of 2026 a majority of the 11 sitting justices were appointed by PT (FSP) presidents: Lula appointed Cármen Lúcia, Dias Toffoli, Cristiano Zanin and Flávio Dino (with Jorge Messias nominated for the seat vacated by Barroso's 2025 retirement); Dilma appointed Luiz Fux and Edson Fachin (the current court president). The rest were appointed by FHC (Gilmar Mendes), Temer (Alexandre de Moraes) and Bolsonaro (Nunes Marques, André Mendonça).",
    "stillServing": "About 7 of the 11 current justices were appointed by FSP (PT) presidents Lula and Dilma — a working majority — as of 2026 (snapshot; the Barroso-seat confirmation was still in process).",
    "verified": true,
